# A package manager's install-time link creation reads two paths it did not
# choose out of every installed manifest's `bin` map: the command name (the
# key) and the script it points at (the value). The consumer walks the map,
# joins each name under the install root's `.bin` directory and each target
# under the package directory, and creates a symlink there (a cmd-shim file on
# Windows). Both joins resolve `..`, so a manifest declaring
# `"bin": {"../../.bashrc": "cli.js"}` or `"bin": {"cli": "../../.bashrc"}`
# makes the installer write outside the project — the advisory's arbitrary
# file overwrite. The fixed revision does not touch the consumers; it adds validation to
# the manifest normalizer the pipeline runs before linking:
#
#   src/util/normalize-manifest/fix.js (vulnerable parent):
#     if (typeof info.name === 'string' && typeof info.bin === 'string' && info.bin.length > 0) {
#       const name = info.name.replace(/^@[^\/]+\//, '');
#       info.bin = {[name]: info.bin};
#     }
#     // ... and, from directories.bin, `bin[scriptName] = path.join('.', binDir, scriptName)`
#
#   src/util/normalize-manifest/fix.js (fix):
#     const VALID_BIN_KEYS = /^[a-z0-9_-]+$/i;
#     ...
#     for (const key of Object.keys(bin)) {
#       const target = bin[key];
#       if (!VALID_BIN_KEYS.test(key) || !isValidBin(target)) {
#         delete bin[key];
#         warn(reporter.lang('invalidBinEntry', info.name, key));
#       } else {
#         bin[key] = path.normalize(target);
#       }
#     }
#
#   src/util/normalize-manifest/util.js (fix):
#     export function isValidBin(bin: string): boolean {
#       return !path.isAbsolute(bin) && !PARENT_PATH.test(path.normalize(bin));
#     }
#
# The consumers stay byte-identical across the fixed revision
# (src/package-linker.js linkSelfDependencies -> linkBin -> fs.symlink/src,
# src/fetchers/base-fetcher.js `${binDest}/${binName}`), so a binding keyed on
# the link creation cannot separate the revisions by construction.
#
# Held at attention, re-measured on the current ruleset. The fix is entirely
# inside the normalizer: `diff -rq` between the fix parent and the fix shows
# exactly three changed files (reporters/lang/en.js, util/normalize-manifest/
# fix.js, util/normalize-manifest/util.js), so both consumers of the bin map
# are byte-identical across it and a consumer-keyed binding cannot separate
# the revisions by construction.
#
#   - three `--cache off` runs per revision of the whole src/ tree (timeout
#     180, --max-ram 6GB): 14 findings on each side under the generic profile
#     and 20 under `-profile library`, stable within a revision and identical
#     across it (the same 22 and 34 location rows). Nothing lands in
#     util/normalize-manifest/fix.js, util/normalize-manifest/util.js,
#     package-linker.js or fetchers/base-fetcher.js; the findings sit in
#     constants.js, fetchers/tarball-fetcher.js, util/fs.js,
#     util/generate-pnp-map-api.tpl.js and util/git.js.
#   - `vyql match` on the normalizer directory, generic and library profiles,
#     both revisions: fix.js carries only the three `require()` DynamicCodeLoad
#     labels (lines 11-13) and nothing at the bin handling. Under the library
#     profile the directory's only difference across the fix is that util.js
#     exports one more function, whose parameter then takes the param-source
#     label.
#   - `fs.symlink` (package-linker.js:43, fetchers/base-fetcher.js:89) and
#     `cmdShim` (package-linker.js:37) carry no label: the generated JavaScript
#     FilePathAccess set covers writeFile/writeFileSync/createWriteStream/
#     rename/mkdir/open/appendFile/unlink/readdir/readFile, not symlink.
#     `vyql trace -from ExternalEntryInput -to FilePathAccess` on
#     package-linker.js under the library profile reports one source, none
#     reaching a sink, dead-ending at linkBin's parameter. Binding the symlink
#     destination as a path sink would fire on both revisions anyway, since
#     the linker is unchanged.
#   - the archive-link binding shipped since binds symlink/symlinkSync/
#     ensureSymlink/createSymlink but requires a tar `linkname` selector and a
#     module-scope containment negation — an archive extractor's shape, not a
#     package-manifest linker's — and does not fire here. The pip twin's
#     concept, code.PackageEntryPointScriptWrite, still has a Python emitter
#     only, so VYQL-PATH-005 cannot fire on JavaScript at all.
#   - atoms re-enumerated on the real fix.js at both revisions: Object.keys,
#     delete, .test(, .startsWith(, path.join and .replace( are all present at
#     the parent — a filename regex at line 221 and license-prefix checks at
#     lines 267/285/314 — so a module- or function-level "no name check"
#     negation is satisfied while the bin entries stay unvalidated. The fixed
#     module's only additions are VALID_BIN_KEYS and its `[a-z0-9_-]` literal,
#     isValidBin, Object.keys(bin), delete bin[key] and path.normalize(target);
#     the two documentation-answerable containment atoms, path.isAbsolute and
#     a parent-path test, live in the sibling module util.js, outside fix.js's
#     module scope, and path.normalize preserves a leading `..` so keying on
#     it credits a non-validating normalizer.
#   - the JavaScript frontend still emits no call-argument tokens (no call_arg
#     in internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/javascript.go), and landing them
#     would still not separate these revisions: the only generic per-argument
#     atom the fix adds is the argument of Object.keys(bin), which is iteration
#     rather than containment, so a negation keyed on it credits a normalizer
#     that walks the map and checks nothing. Which field a guard is applied to
#     stays a non-fact, so a guard for `license` and a guard for `bin` remain
#     indistinguishable in the same module.
#   - `grep -rln --include=*.js '(pkg|manifest|info|json|data|dep)\.bin\b'`
#     across every rank clone under /tmp/cve-work: 11 files besides this rank's
#     own clone, all vendored bundles, release docs or fixtures (one a bundled
#     pre-fix yarn-1.19.1). No independent consumer of the shape exists to test
#     a consumer-side binding against.
#
# Kinship: the pip twin of this weakness class has vocabulary —
# code.PackageEntryPointScriptWrite / VYQL-PATH-005 ("a package can provide an
# entry point name with path separators or parent-directory components").
# pip's fix landed in the consumer and left a documented call inside it, which
# is what that binding keys on; here the fixed revision leaves nothing inside
# the consumer and moved all checking into the normalizer, two pipeline stages
# earlier, behind a name the fixing commit minted. A future binding should
# reuse that concept rather than mint a sibling.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-granularity, all four tests
# rejected. Tests one and two are the normalizer pair, the minimal pair for
# this fix; tests three and four are the consumer pair, the minimal pair for
# the write primitive. When call-argument facts (or an equivalent per-field
# guard attribution) land for JavaScript, test one must flip to
# expect VYQL-PATH-005 and test two must stay reject; with a consumer-side
# route instead, test three must flip and test four stay reject.

test "the manifest normalizer expands bin entries with no name or target validation"
  lang javascript
  file normalize-manifest-fix.js
  reject VYQL-PATH-005
  code
  ```
  const path = require('path');

  export default (async function(
    info: Object,
    moduleLoc: string,
    isRoot: boolean,
    warn: WarnFunction,
    looseSemver: boolean,
  ): Promise<void> {
    // if the `bin` field is as string then expand it to an object with a single property
    // based on the original `bin` field and `name field`
    if (typeof info.name === 'string' && typeof info.bin === 'string' && info.bin.length > 0) {
      const name = info.name.replace(/^@[^\/]+\//, '');
      info.bin = {[name]: info.bin};
    }

    const dirs = info.directories;
    if (dirs && typeof dirs === 'object') {
      const binDir = dirs.bin;
      if (!info.bin && binDir && typeof binDir === 'string') {
        const bin = (info.bin = {});
        const fullBinDir = path.join(moduleLoc, binDir);
        for (const scriptName of await fs.readdir(fullBinDir)) {
          bin[scriptName] = path.join('.', binDir, scriptName);
        }
      }
    }

    // sibling manifest fields already carry the generic validation vocabulary,
    // which is what defeats a module-level "no name check" negation:
    for (const filename of await fs.readdir(moduleLoc)) {
      if (/^(.*?)\.[0-9]$/.test(filename)) {
        continue;
      }
    }
    const lower = info.license.toLowerCase();
    if (lower === 'license' || lower.startsWith('license.') || lower.startsWith('unlicense.')) {
      info.license = lower;
    }
  });
  ```

test "the patched normalizer drops bin entries whose name or target escapes the package"
  lang javascript
  file normalize-manifest-fixed.js
  reject VYQL-PATH-005
  code
  ```
  const path = require('path');

  const VALID_BIN_KEYS = /^[a-z0-9_-]+$/i;

  export default (async function(
    info: Object,
    moduleLoc: string,
    isRoot: boolean,
    warn: WarnFunction,
    looseSemver: boolean,
  ): Promise<void> {
    if (typeof info.name === 'string' && typeof info.bin === 'string' && info.bin.length > 0) {
      const name = info.name.replace(/^@[^\/]+\//, '');
      info.bin = {[name]: info.bin};
    }

    // Validate that the bin entries reference only files within their package, and that
    // their name is a valid file name
    if (typeof info.bin === 'object' && info.bin !== null) {
      const bin: Object = info.bin;
      for (const key of Object.keys(bin)) {
        const target = bin[key];
        if (!VALID_BIN_KEYS.test(key) || !isValidBin(target)) {
          delete bin[key];
          warn(reporter.lang('invalidBinEntry', info.name, key));
        } else {
          bin[key] = path.normalize(target);
        }
      }
    }
  });
  ```

test "the installer joins manifest bin names and targets into link paths"
  lang javascript
  file package-linker.js
  reject VYQL-PATH-005
  code
  ```
  const path = require('path');

  export async function linkBin(src: string, dest: string): Promise<void> {
    if (process.platform === 'win32') {
      await cmdShim(src, dest, {createPwshFile: false});
    } else {
      await fs.mkdirp(path.dirname(dest));
      await fs.symlink(src, dest);
      await fs.chmod(dest, '755');
    }
  }

  export default class PackageLinker {
    async linkSelfDependencies(
      pkg: Manifest,
      pkgLoc: string,
      targetBinLoc: string,
      override: boolean = false,
    ): Promise<void> {
      targetBinLoc = path.join(targetBinLoc, '.bin');
      await fs.mkdirp(targetBinLoc);
      targetBinLoc = await fs.realpath(targetBinLoc);
      pkgLoc = await fs.realpath(pkgLoc);
      for (const [scriptName, scriptCmd] of entries(pkg.bin)) {
        const dest = path.join(targetBinLoc, scriptName);
        const src = path.join(pkgLoc, scriptCmd);
        if (!await fs.exists(src)) {
          if (!override) {
            continue;
          }
        }
        await linkBin(src, dest);
      }
    }
  }
  ```

test "an installer that validates the manifest entry before joining is clean"
  lang javascript
  file package-linker-checked.js
  reject VYQL-PATH-005
  code
  ```
  const path = require('path');

  const VALID_BIN_KEYS = /^[a-z0-9_-]+$/i;

  export default class PackageLinker {
    async linkSelfDependencies(
      pkg: Manifest,
      pkgLoc: string,
      targetBinLoc: string,
      override: boolean = false,
    ): Promise<void> {
      targetBinLoc = path.join(targetBinLoc, '.bin');
      for (const [scriptName, scriptCmd] of entries(pkg.bin)) {
        if (!VALID_BIN_KEYS.test(scriptName) || path.isAbsolute(scriptCmd)) {
          continue;
        }
        const dest = path.join(targetBinLoc, scriptName);
        const src = path.join(pkgLoc, scriptCmd);
        await linkBin(src, dest);
      }
    }
  }
  ```
